'''Zia''' is a [[Papuan languages|Papuan language]] spoken in the Lower [[Waria Valley]] in [[Morobe Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]]. It is part of the Binandere subgroup of the [[Trans–New Guinea languages|Trans–New Guinea]] phylum of languages (Ross, 2005).{{full citation needed|date=August 2025}}

